WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.844
Your first pay stub can be confusing.

2
00:00:03.924 --> 00:00:08.729
The amount you earn isn't the amount
that lands in your account. Here's why.

3
00:00:10.029 --> 00:00:13.691
Gross pay is what you earn
before anything comes out.

4
00:00:13.771 --> 00:00:19.216
Take-home pay, also called net pay,
is what's left after deductions.

5
00:00:19.296 --> 00:00:22.388
That's the money that
actually reaches you.

6
00:00:23.688 --> 00:00:27.923
Here's an example pay stub
with made-up round numbers.

7
00:00:28.003 --> 00:00:30.654
Gross pay is $2,000.

8
00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:34.848
Federal income tax takes $170.

9
00:00:34.928 --> 00:00:40.103
Social Security and Medicare take $153.

10
00:00:40.183 --> 00:00:46.131
Health insurance is $90, and
$80 goes to retirement savings.

11
00:00:46.211 --> 00:00:49.569
Many states also take state income tax.

12
00:00:50.869 --> 00:00:55.140
Add it up, and $493 comes out.

13
00:00:55.220 --> 00:01:02.144
So $2,000 of gross pay becomes
$1,507 of take-home pay.

14
00:01:02.224 --> 00:01:05.679
That's about three quarters
of the gross amount.

15
00:01:06.979 --> 00:01:11.230
That's why a budget starts with
take-home pay, not gross pay.

16
00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:14.851
You can only spend or save
the money that reaches you.

17
00:01:14.931 --> 00:01:18.601
And check each stub, because
deductions can change,

18
00:01:18.641 --> 00:01:20.902
like when you join a health plan.

19
00:01:22.202 --> 00:01:23.622
Quick recap.

20
00:01:23.702 --> 00:01:25.552
Gross pay is what you earn.

21
00:01:25.632 --> 00:01:28.808
Take-home pay is what
lands in your account.

22
00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:33.309
Income tax, Social Security
and Medicare come out first,

23
00:01:33.349 --> 00:01:36.491
and benefits like health
insurance can too.

24
00:01:37.791 --> 00:01:38.841
Quick check.

25
00:01:38.921 --> 00:01:40.658
What is take-home pay?

26
00:01:40.738 --> 00:01:45.200
Answer three short questions below
the video to finish the lesson.

27
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.982
Now find your last pay stub.

28
00:01:49.062 --> 00:01:52.128
In your Money Map, enter your gross pay,

29
00:01:52.168 --> 00:01:55.544
your take-home pay and your
three biggest deductions.
